mpatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Ubuntu 7.10 and kernel 2.6.22-14-generic were observed before work and again after reboot. The repaired program compiled under the installed Python 2.5.1 and operated successfully before and after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a4a8352f19a24503","cmd-5139ea3565f84d2e","cmd-d7aaf25a6e694189","cmd-dce7fb7309ba4d35","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Maintain operational availability and recovery of the repaired service.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy pre-restart service, socket, preserved document, process identity, and successful reader request were captured. The reboot was acknowledged, SSH became temporarily unavailable, the boot ID changed, and the complete service, protocol, roles, data, and access boundary recovered.","evidence_ids":["cmd-87cecefe4455485c","cmd-b48233ca10704083","cmd-70e18ae2db06443a","cmd-e9bee40c65f3491b","cmd-dce7fb7309ba4d35","global:after_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.92,"summary":"All substantive system mutations—account and group provisioning, server repair, permission changes, SysV service installation, enablement, and reboot—had clear task or mandatory restart-evidence purposes. Two low-risk avoidable artifacts remained: server.pyc created during compatibility compilation by cmd-d7aaf25a6e694189, and /tmp/statusd-outsider-post.err created by the final denial test in cmd-dce7fb7309ba4d35. The earlier /tmp/statusd-outsider.err test artifact was removed by the reboot. No unrelated package, platform, or security-control mutations are evident, and package health remained intact.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d7aaf25a6e694189","cmd-1db4d5b5b29f4ad1","cmd-dce7fb7309ba4d35","global:after_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol for the sole managed node is complete and coherent: healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged reboot, independently confirmed changed boot identity, and recovered service, data, identities, protocol, and access controls. Only minor retained validation artifacts reduce operational hygiene.","limitations":["Systemd failed-unit collection was unsupported on this legacy SysV platform, so there is no provider-wide failed-service inventory; direct statusd health checks nevertheless succeeded.","The lifecycle collector inventories network listeners rather than Unix-domain sockets, so socket recovery relies on the direct socket and client probes.","The final lifecycle snapshot does not inventory server.pyc; its retention is established by the executor command output rather than a later cleanup check."]}
